WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.407 --> 00:00:03.147
- [Narrator] Remember
Zoltar, the fortune teller

00:00:03.147 --> 00:00:04.730
from the movie Big?

00:00:05.574 --> 00:00:06.479
The mysterious machine turned

00:00:06.479 --> 00:00:09.062
a young boy’s wish into reality.

00:00:10.090 --> 00:00:11.127
In real life there are hundreds

00:00:11.127 --> 00:00:13.351
of Zoltars all over the country.

00:00:13.351 --> 00:00:16.016
And you can trace them
all back to this guy.

00:00:16.016 --> 00:00:20.156
- My name is Olaf Stanton
and I make Zoltar.

00:00:20.156 --> 00:00:22.739
(magical harp)

00:00:25.712 --> 00:00:27.626
- [Narrator] Olaf runs
Characters Unlimited,

00:00:27.626 --> 00:00:30.048
a company that makes
animated talking characters.

00:00:30.048 --> 00:00:32.375
And one of those machines,
is a fortune teller.

00:00:32.375 --> 00:00:33.865
- The fortune teller is probably

00:00:33.865 --> 00:00:35.072
one of the oldest games there is.

00:00:35.072 --> 00:00:37.578
It's been around since
the turn of the century.

00:00:37.578 --> 00:00:40.180
- [Narrator] Perhaps the
most famous one is Zoltar.

00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:41.792
But, just to be clear, they didn't make

00:00:41.792 --> 00:00:43.401
the one from the movie Big.

00:00:43.401 --> 00:00:46.053
- The Zoltar in the movie Big
was basically a movie prop,

00:00:46.053 --> 00:00:49.384
it was never made to
be a manufactured game.

00:00:49.384 --> 00:00:51.250
Our Zoltar has the talking

00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:53.389
- [Zoltar] Come let Zoltar tell you more!

00:00:53.389 --> 00:00:55.004
- and eye movement and head turning,

00:00:55.004 --> 00:00:57.347
and spits out a card at
the end of the conversation

00:00:57.347 --> 00:01:00.771
and gives you some good words of advice.

00:01:00.771 --> 00:01:03.145
- [Narrator] Every Zoltar
machine is custom made.

00:01:03.145 --> 00:01:05.386
- The first thing we do is
get the cabinet started,

00:01:05.386 --> 00:01:09.475
then we'll cast the head
out of our latex material.

00:01:09.475 --> 00:01:11.845
We put the eyeballs in, we paint the head,

00:01:11.845 --> 00:01:13.630
then it goes to our wig department.

00:01:13.630 --> 00:01:16.650
Zoltar's goatee is put
on, the teeth are put in,

00:01:16.650 --> 00:01:18.056
which are actually my teeth.

00:01:18.056 --> 00:01:19.797
- [Narrator] Wait, they're your teeth?

00:01:19.797 --> 00:01:21.779
- Yes, they're actually my teeth.

00:01:21.779 --> 00:01:23.206
I actually made a mold on my teeth,

00:01:23.206 --> 00:01:27.373
so every Zoltar you see out
there has my teeth in ‘em.

00:01:28.765 --> 00:01:30.193
And then we put all the components in that

00:01:30.193 --> 00:01:31.839
make the card come out, and make it talk

00:01:31.839 --> 00:01:33.925
and give the different messages.

00:01:33.925 --> 00:01:36.425
And then Zoltar's ready to go.

00:01:37.907 --> 00:01:40.784
Although Zoltar is the star
of our fortune teller line,

00:01:40.784 --> 00:01:42.725
he's not the only fortune
teller that we make.

00:01:42.725 --> 00:01:45.967
We have Pappy, we have the old pirate.

00:01:45.967 --> 00:01:49.056
- [Narrator] And those
fortunes, that's Olaf too.

00:01:49.056 --> 00:01:50.437
- We try to make all of our fortunes

00:01:50.437 --> 00:01:53.983
on the lighter side, good
words of wisdom and advice.

00:01:53.983 --> 00:01:56.391
I think one of my favorite is, “Sometimes

00:01:56.391 --> 00:01:58.037
it's better to say too little than to

00:01:58.037 --> 00:01:59.946
say too much and regret it later.”

00:01:59.946 --> 00:02:01.098
There’s a lot of good words of wisdom

00:02:01.098 --> 00:02:02.472
that come out of Zoltar.

00:02:02.472 --> 00:02:03.899
I think people just like to see

00:02:03.899 --> 00:02:05.349
something that they can relate to

00:02:05.349 --> 00:02:08.651
and say, oh yeah how did you
know that, that's so cool.

00:02:08.651 --> 00:02:11.234
It really does bring out
the child in all of us

00:02:11.234 --> 00:02:13.751
to see your fortune on a card.

00:02:13.751 --> 00:02:14.662
- [Narrator] Unless of course you're

00:02:14.662 --> 00:02:16.482
talking about Tom Hanks in the movie Big,

00:02:16.482 --> 00:02:19.315
'cause he gets well, ya know, Big.

